Word frequency lists ru.txt.gz and en.txt.gz

Derived from wordfreq 3.1.1 (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq) by Robyn Speer:
the top words of each language with their Zipf frequency, filtered to plain words.

The wordfreq data is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International license (CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
It is built from Wikipedia, OPUS OpenSubtitles, SUBTLEX, Google Books Ngrams, NewsCrawl,
GlobalVoices, Reddit, Twitter and other sources listed in the wordfreq README.

These two files are distributed under the same CC BY-SA 4.0 license.
The rest of Halfword is under the MIT license (see LICENSE in the repository root).
Rebuild: tools/build_lexicon.py
